contracts.description:
List actual host processes with bounded PID pagination and start identities, not only runtime jobs. Operator hosts only. Command arguments are omitted to avoid exposing secrets. This tool is part of plugin `HeptaRuntime Mac Controller`.

MCP server instructions: Filesystem tools. File lines render as `N:hh|content`; `N:hh` is the line id edit tools target, and edit results are diffs with fresh ids, so edits chain without re-viewing files. Reuse returned content and ids; read complete relevant blocks, then act on them. Each response costs a round trip: first decide what you need next, then request every call that doesn't depend on another's result in that one response.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__heptaruntime_mac_controller_host_processes(args: {
  after_pid?: number;
  host: string;
  // At most 128 process records per response.
  limit?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Start a bounded background file-name or content search under one configured read root. Omitted options preserve case-sensitive literal matching; explicit query_mode selects literal, regex or file glob. Supports case folding, file/exclusion globs, context lines and early exact-name termination. DOCX/XLSX text is extracted under expansion limits; PDF requires the administrator-configured host interpreter with a bounded pypdf parser. Skipped formats and limits are explicit in statistics. No shell or arbitrary targets. Refuses symlinks and hard links; skips binary content and bounds traversal, bytes, results and time. HTTP ownership is the verified private operator credential, shared by all its users; stdio ownership remains this native session. Never takes caller-selected ownership. The same HTTP credential can resume retained metadata and immutable terminal pages after reconnect or controller restart only while the current host binding and read-root policy authorize access; unfinished searches become interrupted without relaunch. Not authenticated ChatGPT caller isolation or running-program resume. Regex uses bounded Python syntax; glob filters do not imply gitignore parity. This tool is part of plugin `HeptaRuntime Mac Controller`.

